# Trust-root governance files — require code owner approval before merge to main
# Without this, a single PR can edit covenant.sh/covenantwin.py + regenerate its own integrity pin,
# weakening the covenant. These must be reviewed by a human every time they change.
#
# GitHub only honors a CODEOWNERS file at the true repo root (or its .github/) — this file
# lives there for that reason, covering both platform subdirectories with root-relative paths.
#
# Two sets of paths are covered below:
#  1. This repo's OWN trust root (CovenantMac/templates/, CovenantMac/install.sh, CovenantWin/src/, the
#     shared v1_release/, etc.) — the files that actually exist here and that a malicious or
#     careless PR could weaken.
#  2. The paths each platform's installer writes into a governed TARGET repo (.githooks/,
#     .claude/*, etc.) — these don't exist in this repo; listed as guidance mirrored into
#     every installed repo's own CODEOWNERS scaffold.

# ── This repo's real trust root ──────────────────────────────────────────────
v1_release/                         @Lakshya5876
CovenantMac/templates/                  @Lakshya5876
CovenantMac/install.sh                  @Lakshya5876
CovenantMac/uninstall.sh                @Lakshya5876
CovenantMac/.github/workflows/          @Lakshya5876
CovenantWin/src/                        @Lakshya5876
CovenantWin/install.ps1                 @Lakshya5876
CovenantWin/uninstall.ps1               @Lakshya5876
.github/workflows/                  @Lakshya5876

# ── Paths that only exist in a governed TARGET repo (reference only) ────────
# Git hooks — the enforcement layer
.githooks/                          @your-org/platform-team

# Bash/PowerShell guard hook — prevents agent from disarming itself
.claude/hooks/                      @your-org/platform-team

# Covenant integrity manifest — pins every governance file's hash
.claude/covenant_integrity.sha256       @your-org/platform-team

# CI governance workflow — authoritative backstop if local hooks are stripped
.github/workflows/covenant.yml          @your-org/platform-team

# Covenant state + ledger — token budgets, receipts, audit log
.claude/covenant_state.json             @your-org/platform-team

# Debt ratchet — technical debt baseline
.claude/baseline.json               @your-org/platform-team

# Repo constitution — rules Claude Code must follow
CLAUDE.md                           @your-org/platform-team

# Claude Code permissions — what the agent is allowed to do
.claude/settings.json               @your-org/platform-team

# MCP server configuration — which external tools Claude Code connects to
.mcp.json                           @your-org/platform-team
